                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "-\\frac15",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", then point-gradient form.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The given gradient is $5$. Perpendicular gradients have product $-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}m&=-\\frac15\\\\y-4&=-\\frac15(x+8)\\\\5y-20&=-x-8\\\\y&=-\\frac15x+\\frac{12}{5}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
